# AlphaCipher .gitattributes
#
# Policy: treat every file in the repository as binary.  Git stores the
# bytes verbatim, performs no line-ending normalization on commit or on
# checkout, and produces no textual diffs.  This is the only setting
# that guarantees byte-for-byte fidelity across the mixed-line-ending
# tree we ship (CRLF Visual Studio sources alongside LF Makefile / shell
# / Eagle / Markdown).
#
# The `-text` attribute on `*` overrides core.autocrlf and any
# inherited text-vs-binary heuristic, so this works the same on
# Windows, macOS, and Linux working copies.
#
# Trade-off: `git diff` will print "Binary files differ" rather than a
# textual diff.  Use `git diff --text -- <path>` to force a textual
# view of a specific file on demand.

* -text
